# C++20 Core and Tests Rules

- Separate headless logic (`kmedia_core`) from Qt Quick UI (`src/app/ApplicationController`). Never include QML headers inside `src/core/`, `src/media/`, `src/models/`, `src/parsers/`, `src/network/`, or `src/integrations/`.
- Match `.clang-format` and `.clang-tidy`: `CamelCase` classes/structs/enums, `camelCase` methods/variables, `m_` member prefix.
- Avoid narrowing conversions or sign warnings (`-Wconversion -Wsign-conversion` are enabled in `cmake/CompilerWarnings.cmake`).
- Never block the UI thread or introduce polling loops in steady state; use async Qt signals, SQLite WAL transactions, and OS filesystem notifications.
- Write Catch2 unit tests under `tests/` for all new core logic and run `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen ctest --preset <preset> --output-on-failure`.
